WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:04.170
Welcome to your second drink of two weeks.

2
00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:05.850
This is a fun episode.

3
00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.930
You guys, we tried scotch and Splenda in this episode.

4
00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:09.570
I know.

5
00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:11.110
Jenna, you brought it all in.

6
00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:11.670
I know.

7
00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:14.910
I don't want to ruin it for anyone who might be listening for the first time,

8
00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:17.470
but I reflect very fondly on that.

9
00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:20.210
Also, it was so early in the morning.

10
00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:21.150
It was really early.

11
00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:22.650
It was a little crazy.

12
00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:27.070
We also talk about how much we wanted to interview Idris Elba for the podcaSt.

13
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:28.710
Yes, and we still do.

14
00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:32.490
This reminded me that we need to still try and make that happen.

15
00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:34.990
I want us to put it on our manifest board.

16
00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:36.790
Well, the last time we checked in with him,

17
00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:40.890
his people said he was on a set somewhere for five months.

18
00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:42.750
Yeah, I can't remember what that movie was.

19
00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:43.590
He's very busy.

20
00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:48.130
He's very busy, but, you know, maybe when the five-month project ends, Idris,

21
00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:50.950
you would like to come into the Office Lady's studio.

22
00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:51.490
Yes.

23
00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:55.470
All right, well, listen, I have a quick bit of extra trivia for this episode.

24
00:00:56.030 --> 00:01:01.590
It was originally titled Two Weeks Notice, and then it got changed to Two Weeks.

25
00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:04.410
Do you think that's because of the movie Two Weeks Notice?

26
00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:07.750
You know, the one with Hugh Grant and Sandra Bullock, Two Weeks Notice?

27
00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:08.830
Do you remember that rom-com?

28
00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:13.550
I mean, I remember hearing of it.

29
00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:14.570
I did not see it.

30
00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:14.930
Oh.

31
00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:16.290
Have you seen it?

32
00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:16.570
Yeah.

33
00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:18.190
I went through a Hugh Grant thing.

34
00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:24.170
I was like, he is the funniest person I've seen in a long time in movies.

35
00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:28.890
And what's crazy is I was just flying, and I watched Notting Hill again.

36
00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:29.990
I love Notting Hill.

37
00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:31.270
Oh, stop it.

38
00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:33.750
I mean, I've seen that movie so many times.

39
00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:34.230
The bench.

40
00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:34.830
The bench.

41
00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:35.450
All of it.

42
00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:35.600
I know.

43
00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:36.470
Well, anyway.

44
00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:39.170
That dinner party is one of the best scenes.

45
00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:41.390
I would love to be in that dinner party scene.

46
00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:42.250
So good.

47
00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:44.090
And yes, it's Hugh Grant.

48
00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:44.870
It's Two Weeks Notice.

49
00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:46.490
It's like Hugh Grant is doing it.

50
00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:48.050
It's just, you know, now.

51
00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:48.850
You know what?

52
00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:50.090
I feel like it was a decision.

53
00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:50.370
Here.

54
00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:52.950
I am completely spitballing here, guys.

55
00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:54.750
There could be zero truth to this.

56
00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:55.050
Okay.

57
00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:58.030
I feel like this is like something a network suit would say.

58
00:01:58.190 --> 00:02:01.730
They'd be like, you can't name the episode Two Weeks Notice because there's already a movie

59
00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:02.190
named that.

60
00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:02.950
You know what?

61
00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:07.050
I actually had a whole other thing in my brain.

62
00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:07.790
What was that?

63
00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:08.870
Here's what I imagined.

64
00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:12.950
I imagined a bunch of dudes in the writer's room calling it Two Weeks Notice.

65
00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:15.370
And then Mindy Kaling walking in.

66
00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:16.810
Mindy Kaling, like…

67
00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:17.730
Loves a rom-com.

68
00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:18.610
Loves a rom-com.

69
00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:20.130
And she's like, what are you doing?

70
00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:21.410
That's already a thing.

71
00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:23.390
And I feel like she had to school everybody.

72
00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:23.890
Okay.

73
00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:25.170
This was my imagination.

74
00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:26.390
I like both of these theories.

75
00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:26.810
Okay.

76
00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:27.670
All right.

77
00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:30.570
Well, we also got this letter about a favorite moment from the episode.

78
00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:31.790
It's from Danny H.

79
00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:33.170
in Duluth, Minnesota.

80
00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:34.430
Danny says,

81
00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:35.270
Hi, office ladies.

82
00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:39.950
My favorite scene from this episode is actually a scene added back into the superfan episode.

83
00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:42.350
It's when Michael and Toby are in the break room.

84
00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:47.070
Michael is asking Toby for advice on what to do with his life and what his resume should

85
00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:47.510
look like.

86
00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:52.290
I did not expect to be so tickled by this scene, but towards the end when Michael is speaking

87
00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:57.510
directly to the film crew as if he's saying some inspirational monologue in a movie, and

88
00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.790
it just makes me wheeze.

89
00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:02.590
Please, please, please touch on this scene as it is a gem.

90
00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:05.230
Well, we love this scene selection, Danny.

91
00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:05.930
And you know what?

92
00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:07.190
I think we should share it.

93
00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:08.530
I'm going to set it up for everyone.

94
00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:13.410
Michael is coming to terms with the fact that he has put in his two weeks notice, and

95
00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:17.410
he's kind of freaking out about that fact, and he doesn't have a plan for the future.

96
00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:21.150
And he goes back to the annex, and he's going to get advice from Toby.

97
00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:23.010
Like you said, let's hear it.

98
00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.900
Hey, Toby, I have a real quick question for you.

99
00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:29.780
Sure.

100
00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:33.840
What should your resume be, and what should you do with your life?

101
00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:34.320
Okay.

102
00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:37.500
Two questions, I guess.

103
00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:37.820
Fine.

104
00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:39.520
No, no, no.

105
00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:40.640
I'm sticking to what I said.

106
00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:43.180
One question with two parts.

107
00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:46.240
Okay, well, look, the second part, you know, that's really personal.

108
00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:47.520
I mean, only you can answer that.

109
00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:48.760
So you're trying to get out of it.

110
00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:49.300
God.

111
00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:52.100
Thanks for your help, moron.

112
00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:54.540
Okay, well, look, the resumes.

113
00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:55.840
I can really help you there.

114
00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:56.800
I must read 20 today.

115
00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:57.380
Okay.

116
00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:58.500
Good.

117
00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:04.060
Write this down.

118
00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:10.660
Born in a medium-sized town, Michael Gary Scott always knew he was different.

119
00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:13.760
Okay, so we might start with, say, your most recent thing.

120
00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.160
Summary of achievements.

121
00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:16.920
What have you done here at Dunder Mifflin?

122
00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:18.280
Changed things.

123
00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:23.060
Ushered in a new era of love and comedy in the workplace.

124
00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:25.580
Hired many.

125
00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:26.760
Fired few.

126
00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:27.740
Fired few.

127
00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:28.140
Made money.

128
00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:29.280
Lost money.

129
00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:32.000
Learned to stop counting.

130
00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:37.070
This is our moment.

131
00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:39.960
This is our time.

132
00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:45.350
This next part should be sung, if possible.

133
00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:48.090
That's Michael's resume.

134
00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:49.310
It's brilliant.

135
00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:50.250
It is brilliant.

136
00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:53.890
I don't know how Paul Lieberstein made it through that without laughing.

137
00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:58.930
Because for me, the thing that always got me with Steve is how, as Michael, he would

138
00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:00.010
take these pauses.

139
00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:00.410
Yes.

140
00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:01.930
And then say something ridiculous.

141
00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:03.230
Yes, he takes his time.

142
00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:04.130
You don't know what's coming.

143
00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:05.090
No, no.

144
00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:09.650
Well, I really have to thank Danny for suggesting that we go back and watch that scene because

145
00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:10.750
it's really awesome.

146
00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:14.450
And because of Danny's letter, I ended up watching the whole superfan version.

147
00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:17.570
And I'd like to offer another scene that was added back.

148
00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:19.310
It's between Michael and Daryl.

149
00:05:20.150 --> 00:05:25.410
So, after Michael realizes he's not going to get a job someplace else, he gets his idea

150
00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:27.230
to start his own paper company.

151
00:05:27.230 --> 00:05:32.070
And he goes down to Daryl's office for advice on starting his own company.

152
00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:37.390
When Michael needs something from Daryl, it's maybe one of my favorite dynamics.

153
00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:42.230
It's like this superfan episode has a Michael Toby and it has a Michael Daryl.

154
00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:44.490
So, I think we need to hear Michael and Daryl.

155
00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:47.260
Hey, Double D.

156
00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:48.520
What's up, Mike?

157
00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:49.600
Michael.

158
00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:54.380
Hey, if you'll just excuse us for a sec.

159
00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:56.660
You know what?

160
00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:57.280
You could stay.

161
00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:58.860
Why don't we, this is good.

162
00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:00.320
I just had a question.

163
00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:02.240
You guys work in a warehouse.

164
00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:08.800
How much warehouse space do you think a paper company would need if it had, like, 25 clients?

165
00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:10.880
Hoping someday to expand.

166
00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:14.160
Maybe, like, a garage?

167
00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:16.160
Would you start your own company?

168
00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:18.160
No.

169
00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:18.940
Can I have this?

170
00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:19.780
Yes.

171
00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:20.340
Can I invest?

172
00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:20.900
Yeah.

173
00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:23.240
My money's tied up.

174
00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:23.820
I'll tap down.

175
00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:24.900
Shoot!

176
00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:25.720
Darn it.

177
00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:26.840
It'll sound like a sure thing.

178
00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:27.980
Oh, doesn't it?

179
00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:31.680
Mike, I don't want to answer all your questions, but I need you to know something.

180
00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:33.340
I'm messing with you.

181
00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:35.800
This doesn't sound like a good idea.

182
00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:36.560
Understood.

183
00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:41.120
He wants to start his own company, and I was just trying to dissuade him.

184
00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:42.940
I tried.

185
00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:45.440
I honestly tried.

186
00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:48.710
So there you go.

187
00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:53.670
Michael trying to get some advice on starting his paper company.

188
00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:56.230
How much space does he need for all the paper?

189
00:06:56.230 --> 00:07:00.370
I like that Daryl really earnestly tried to talk him out of it.

190
00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:00.730
I know.

191
00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:02.310
Oh, man.

192
00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:06.830
Well, this superfan also has a great runner of talking heads of people giving their opinion

193
00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:07.730
on Michael leaving.

194
00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:12.390
They come after Hank leads Michael out of the office, and they watch him drive away.

195
00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:18.010
The broadcast version has a single Oscar talking head, but in the superfan version, a lot

196
00:07:18.010 --> 00:07:19.910
more of us weigh in, and it was fun.

197
00:07:20.130 --> 00:07:20.710
Let's listen.

198
00:07:23.090 --> 00:07:28.070
And just like that, as mysteriously as he arrived, he was gone.

199
00:07:28.930 --> 00:07:30.830
I would like to say that I will miss him.

200
00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:35.380
I would like to say that.

201
00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:38.640
I'll miss him when he dies.

202
00:07:38.980 --> 00:07:41.660
I'm not going to spend energy missing him every step of the way.

203
00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:43.520
I'll miss Michael.

204
00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:45.460
But have you seen this new guy?

205
00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:48.540
When God closes a door, he opens a window.

206
00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:50.160
You feel what I mean?

207
00:07:52.850 --> 00:07:54.810
Old Creed outlives yet another boss.

208
00:07:55.970 --> 00:07:57.510
Time to put a marble in the box.

209
00:08:02.130 --> 00:08:07.730
So I guess Creed has a box on his desk, and it's filled with marbles for every boss he

210
00:08:07.730 --> 00:08:09.050
outlives or lasts.

211
00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:10.450
That's so great.

212
00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:12.070
There were like five marbles in there.

213
00:08:12.390 --> 00:08:12.870
Five.

214
00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:15.070
Oh, my gosh.

215
00:08:15.110 --> 00:08:16.210
That's really funny to me.

216
00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:19.470
Well, Angela Martin also had a candy bag alt.

217
00:08:19.590 --> 00:08:21.510
Which we shot, and it went like this.

218
00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:23.850
I don't know what lies in Michael's future.

219
00:08:24.110 --> 00:08:28.710
He's an able-bodied man with a formal education, so I'm sure he'll survive.

220
00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:33.570
Truthfully, though, I wouldn't be surprised to find him begging outside of my church in

221
00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:34.050
a few years.

222
00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:37.110
I can see him now with this little misspelled sign.

223
00:08:37.770 --> 00:08:41.090
I love that his sign is misspelled in Angela's fantasy.

224
00:08:41.190 --> 00:08:42.410
She's just such a bitch.

225
00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:43.850
Oh, listen.

226
00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:47.230
Bottom line, the super fan version of this one is really great.

227
00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:49.490
You get, like, whole extra scenes.

228
00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:55.610
There's also this great added Michael talking head, but where he reveals he has a pet gecko.

229
00:08:55.610 --> 00:08:57.210
I highly recommend it.

230
00:08:57.350 --> 00:08:59.450
I saw people write in about the gecko.

231
00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:03.410
A few people wanted to know, if Michael had a gecko, what would he have named it?

232
00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:04.750
And I was like, I don't know.

233
00:09:06.030 --> 00:09:06.930
All right, everyone.

234
00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:09.510
We hope you enjoy your second drink of two weeks.

235
00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:14.520
I'm Jenna Fisher.

236
00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:15.840
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

237
00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:17.120
We were on The Office together.

238
00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:18.360
And we're best friends.

239
00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:22.200
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.

240
00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:26.560
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes

241
00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:29.180
stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

242
00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:30.320
We're The Office ladies.

243
00:09:34.410 --> 00:09:35.370
Oh, good.

244
00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:37.790
I always want to say good morning.

245
00:09:37.790 --> 00:09:40.150
I know you do, because it's 9.30 a.m.

246
00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:40.570
for us.

247
00:09:40.570 --> 00:09:42.030
I know, and I'm having a cup of tea.

248
00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:43.710
I'm having a cup of coffee.

249
00:09:44.530 --> 00:09:45.570
Hi, guys!

250
00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:53.150
Today, we are talking about two weeks, which is Season 5, Episode 21, written by Erin Schur

251
00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:55.430
and directed by Paul Lieberstein.

252
00:09:55.870 --> 00:10:01.230
As we were warming up today here in the studio, literally warming up because it was very cold.

253
00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:02.450
Yeah, it's freezing in here.

254
00:10:02.650 --> 00:10:04.670
And we were waiting for it to warm up.

255
00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:07.390
We were talking about how much we love writer Erin Schur.

256
00:10:07.390 --> 00:10:09.250
Yes, Erin, you are delightful.

257
00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:12.910
We are enjoying all your emails and just reconnecting with you.

258
00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:14.590
And you have the best stories.

259
00:10:14.810 --> 00:10:15.730
The best stories.

260
00:10:15.750 --> 00:10:20.190
It's no wonder they use so many stories from his real life in episodes.

261
00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:21.790
Here's a summary.

262
00:10:22.070 --> 00:10:27.190
