00:53:46.280 --> 00:53:51.660
And Oscar immediately starts offering very practical advice about how most new businesses

1279
00:53:51.660 --> 00:53:53.980
don't turn a profit for the first two years.

1280
00:53:54.560 --> 00:53:57.000
And, you know, can he afford that?

1281
00:53:57.160 --> 00:53:59.520
Can he afford to make no money for two years?

1282
00:53:59.520 --> 00:54:00.260
Right.

1283
00:54:00.560 --> 00:54:02.880
Well, Michael's like, hey, hey, stop convincing me.

1284
00:54:02.980 --> 00:54:04.040
You got the job.

1285
00:54:05.060 --> 00:54:07.040
With all your number lingo.

1286
00:54:07.740 --> 00:54:09.840
But ultimately, Oscar's a no.

1287
00:54:10.140 --> 00:54:15.480
And that means that he has to move on to Stanley, who he's going to stalk outside the bathroom.

1288
00:54:15.800 --> 00:54:16.240
Outside?

1289
00:54:16.580 --> 00:54:17.540
He's inside.

1290
00:54:17.540 --> 00:54:19.040
I guess outside the stall.

1291
00:54:19.460 --> 00:54:24.080
I don't know how urinals work, but I imagine he walked up while he was just peeing.

1292
00:54:24.240 --> 00:54:26.380
Because Stanley's like, I'm urinating.

1293
00:54:26.880 --> 00:54:28.160
Michael keeps talking to him.

1294
00:54:28.160 --> 00:54:29.080
Stanley's like, no.

1295
00:54:29.700 --> 00:54:32.840
Michael has then a very sad talking head where he's like, you know what?

1296
00:54:32.960 --> 00:54:35.420
No one said yes to prom, but I still had a good time.

1297
00:54:36.120 --> 00:54:36.820
Guess what?

1298
00:54:37.140 --> 00:54:37.360
What?

1299
00:54:38.560 --> 00:54:39.940
Pam fixed the copier.

1300
00:54:40.120 --> 00:54:42.420
After four hours, she did it.

1301
00:54:42.520 --> 00:54:43.440
She didn't let it beat her.

1302
00:54:43.760 --> 00:54:44.720
No, she did not.

1303
00:54:44.820 --> 00:54:46.940
She knows everything about this machine.

1304
00:54:47.480 --> 00:54:49.320
Phyllis is going to copy a piece of paper.

1305
00:54:49.660 --> 00:54:51.580
And Pam is like, did it work?

1306
00:54:51.780 --> 00:54:52.720
How is it?

1307
00:54:52.860 --> 00:54:54.800
And Phyllis is like, fine.

1308
00:54:55.960 --> 00:54:56.400
Fine.

1309
00:54:56.400 --> 00:55:00.620
So this whole copier storyline felt very familiar to me.

1310
00:55:00.820 --> 00:55:08.940
Having worked many temp jobs, having fixed many copiers in my real life, and it just felt

1311
00:55:08.940 --> 00:55:13.980
to me like it was written by someone who also had this personal knowledge.

1312
00:55:14.440 --> 00:55:14.820
Yeah.

1313
00:55:14.820 --> 00:55:19.380
So I had to ask Aaron, have you had experience with copiers?

1314
00:55:19.800 --> 00:55:24.120
You know, because so many of his real life stories have wound up in our scripts, like

1315
00:55:24.120 --> 00:55:25.760
running past the speed meter.

1316
00:55:25.960 --> 00:55:26.200
Yeah.

1317
00:55:26.340 --> 00:55:28.660
And this whole copier story has so many details.

1318
00:55:29.100 --> 00:55:31.600
So as it turns out, yes.

1319
00:55:32.040 --> 00:55:32.520
Yes.

1320
00:55:32.520 --> 00:55:37.040
He told us that he temped in a ton of offices when he was a struggling standup in New York,

1321
00:55:37.040 --> 00:55:42.860
and he quickly learned that if you could unjam the copier, you held the power.

1322
00:55:43.120 --> 00:55:43.820
Yeah.

1323
00:55:44.100 --> 00:55:50.620
He actually said, quote, you were like an office magician, a David Copperfield opening

1324
00:55:50.620 --> 00:55:52.240
the cabinet of mysteries.

1325
00:55:52.760 --> 00:55:59.080
And only a person who has done the copier thing, I feel like totally gets it.

1326
00:55:59.080 --> 00:56:00.260
So I totally get it.

1327
00:56:00.620 --> 00:56:06.600
He said that he would actually copy the user manuals and take them home and read them over

1328
00:56:06.600 --> 00:56:06.920
the week.

1329
00:56:06.920 --> 00:56:09.420
That's the part that really got me.

1330
00:56:09.640 --> 00:56:12.540
He would like learn everything from the manual.

1331
00:56:13.160 --> 00:56:14.240
Aaron, I feel you.

1332
00:56:14.480 --> 00:56:18.380
Thank you for writing this runner for Pam, because I was able to draw on a lot of my real

1333
00:56:18.380 --> 00:56:22.260
life experience when it came to performing this copier story.

1334
00:56:22.720 --> 00:56:23.620
Well, I don't know.

1335
00:56:23.700 --> 00:56:27.760
Did Michael leave the fakie order form in the copier?

1336
00:56:27.760 --> 00:56:28.960
Charles finds it.

1337
00:56:29.100 --> 00:56:29.920
How does he find it?

1338
00:56:30.000 --> 00:56:30.700
We don't know.

1339
00:56:30.840 --> 00:56:35.080
But he's going to get Hank, and they're going to escort him out the building.

1340
00:56:36.040 --> 00:56:37.020
I am sorry.

1341
00:56:37.320 --> 00:56:44.360
I am not sure that there is a recurring character that I love more than Hugh Dane as Hank.

1342
00:56:44.360 --> 00:56:44.540
I know.

1343
00:56:44.740 --> 00:56:45.220
I know.

1344
00:56:45.360 --> 00:56:48.500
When Michael's like, Hank, come on, escort Charles out.

1345
00:56:48.620 --> 00:56:50.160
And Hank's like, come on, man.

1346
00:56:50.260 --> 00:56:50.740
I know.

1347
00:56:50.880 --> 00:56:51.500
Just come on.

1348
00:56:53.220 --> 00:56:54.380
He's so good.

1349
00:56:54.780 --> 00:56:55.580
So good.

1350
00:56:57.940 --> 00:56:59.900
Charles is not going to have that.

1351
00:57:00.100 --> 00:57:02.720
And everyone watches him as he leaves.

1352
00:57:03.100 --> 00:57:06.840
And he's like yelling things from his car, right?

1353
00:57:06.920 --> 00:57:08.260
He's yelling from the parking lot.

1354
00:57:08.320 --> 00:57:09.320
And everyone's looking down.

1355
00:57:09.440 --> 00:57:10.780
And they're like, what's he saying?

1356
00:57:10.780 --> 00:57:12.060
We can't hear what he's saying.

1357
00:57:12.320 --> 00:57:14.000
This is what it said in the script.

1358
00:57:14.340 --> 00:57:14.700
All right.

1359
00:57:15.260 --> 00:57:16.800
Michael walks toward his car.

1360
00:57:17.320 --> 00:57:19.420
Everybody watches from the conference room above.

1361
00:57:19.760 --> 00:57:23.280
Michael stops at his car and looks up at the Dunder Mifflin windows.

1362
00:57:23.280 --> 00:57:25.580
And then he yells this.

1363
00:57:26.100 --> 00:57:26.960
This is it.

1364
00:57:27.120 --> 00:57:28.040
This is goodbye.

1365
00:57:28.360 --> 00:57:28.820
Forever.

1366
00:57:29.340 --> 00:57:29.720
Ah!

1367
00:57:30.320 --> 00:57:31.900
It's such a nice day out here.

1368
00:57:32.260 --> 00:57:32.780
Freedom!

1369
00:57:33.580 --> 00:57:34.380
I'm all right.

1370
00:57:45.620 --> 00:57:47.380
That is what was in the script.

1371
00:57:47.560 --> 00:57:50.820
And then it says he screeches his tires and drives off.

1372
00:57:50.980 --> 00:57:52.440
The camera follows his car.

1373
00:57:52.920 --> 00:57:56.980
Michael parks just a short distance around the corner, gets out of his car, sneaks back

1374
00:57:56.980 --> 00:57:58.900
into the parking lot and into the building.

1375
00:58:00.020 --> 00:58:03.080
We get to hear a lot of people's opinions on Michael leaving.

1376
00:58:03.300 --> 00:58:04.780
My favorite is probably Toby.

1377
00:58:05.280 --> 00:58:05.580
Mm-hmm.

1378
00:58:06.100 --> 00:58:08.740
He says, Michael is like a movie on a plane.

1379
00:58:09.060 --> 00:58:11.520
Not great, but something to watch.

1380
00:58:11.880 --> 00:58:14.160
And then when the movie's over, you're like, now what?

1381
00:58:14.500 --> 00:58:14.900
Yes.

1382
00:58:15.200 --> 00:58:16.620
BJ wrote that talking head.

1383
00:58:16.800 --> 00:58:17.340
Very funny.

1384
00:58:17.780 --> 00:58:20.600
And we got a piece of mail about it.

1385
00:58:20.780 --> 00:58:20.980
What?

1386
00:58:21.200 --> 00:58:26.180
Someone wrote in, and I'm so sorry, I did not write down your name, to say that a missed

1387
00:58:26.180 --> 00:58:31.640
opportunity in this episode was Toby conducting Michael's exit interview.

1388
00:58:32.500 --> 00:58:32.640
Oh.

1389
00:58:33.280 --> 00:58:34.440
Wouldn't you have loved to see that?

1390
00:58:34.580 --> 00:58:38.900
And I mentioned it to Aaron, and Aaron said, oh, but he was escorted out.

1391
00:58:39.100 --> 00:58:44.400
They like to believe that if Michael hadn't been escorted out, he would have had his exit

1392
00:58:44.400 --> 00:58:46.900
interview with Toby before he left.

1393
00:58:47.040 --> 00:58:51.200
Plus, they had written a pretty great Michael-Toby scene where Toby helps him with his resume

1394
00:58:51.200 --> 00:58:52.600
that didn't make it in.

1395
00:58:52.740 --> 00:58:53.060
Yes.

1396
00:58:53.960 --> 00:58:59.740
Well, as everyone is having these really funny talking heads, Creed had one that was in the

1397
00:58:59.740 --> 00:59:02.840
shooting draft, and it didn't make it in, and I have to read it to you.

1398
00:59:03.020 --> 00:59:03.240
Okay.

1399
00:59:03.860 --> 00:59:07.600
Creed says, old Creedie outlives yet another boss.

1400
00:59:07.780 --> 00:59:09.340
Time to put a marble in the box.

1401
00:59:09.960 --> 00:59:14.300
And then Creed pulls out a cigar box out from his desk and puts a marble in it.

1402
00:59:14.420 --> 00:59:17.000
There are four marbles in that box.

1403
00:59:22.700 --> 00:59:23.740
Isn't that amazing?

1404
00:59:24.140 --> 00:59:26.820
Well, like you said, Angela, Michael is not leaving.

1405
00:59:28.200 --> 00:59:33.500
He actually army crawls through the front door, through the office.

1406
00:59:34.400 --> 00:59:36.280
He goes over to accounting.

1407
00:59:37.300 --> 00:59:39.640
This was a really fun scene for us to shoot.

1408
00:59:39.800 --> 00:59:41.440
It was really hard not to laugh.

1409
00:59:41.860 --> 00:59:46.260
We played around with how I shut the drawer, and I ultimately shut it with my foot, and it

1410
00:59:46.260 --> 00:59:47.660
was just like so fun.

1411
00:59:48.520 --> 00:59:51.120
Steve really tore up his elbows and his knees, though.

1412
00:59:51.340 --> 00:59:51.600
Yeah.

1413
00:59:51.600 --> 00:59:52.200
Doing that.

1414
00:59:52.380 --> 00:59:53.760
He got like a rug burn.

1415
00:59:53.960 --> 00:59:54.380
Yes.

1416
00:59:54.620 --> 00:59:58.460
And Randy told us that they offered him elbow and knee pads.

1417
00:59:58.660 --> 00:59:58.940
Uh-huh.

1418
00:59:59.020 --> 01:00:00.240
And Steve was like, it's fine.

1419
01:00:00.240 --> 01:00:00.880
I'll do it.

1420
01:00:00.940 --> 01:00:05.340
And he did two takes without the elbow and knee pads, and he totally tore up his elbows

1421
01:00:05.340 --> 01:00:05.760
and knees.

1422
01:00:05.860 --> 01:00:06.640
He was so committed.

1423
01:00:07.340 --> 01:00:11.540
Also, Randy told us, you know when he throws that highlighter?

1424
01:00:11.900 --> 01:00:12.460
At gym?

1425
01:00:12.600 --> 01:00:12.880
Yeah.

1426
01:00:13.020 --> 01:00:13.180
Yeah.

1427
01:00:13.180 --> 01:00:14.860
That was not a real highlighter.

1428
01:00:15.020 --> 01:00:16.500
That was a fakie highlighter.

1429
01:00:16.840 --> 01:00:18.680
Oh, so it wouldn't like hurt someone?

1430
01:00:18.900 --> 01:00:19.300
Yes.

1431
01:00:19.480 --> 01:00:21.920
Remember when Michael throws the pen at Toby's forehead?

1432
01:00:22.100 --> 01:00:23.740
And Phil had to make a rubber pen?

1433
01:00:23.840 --> 01:00:23.980
Yeah.

1434
01:00:24.420 --> 01:00:28.160
Phil had to make a rubber highlighter, and it cost $850.

1435
01:00:28.900 --> 01:00:29.300
Whoa.

1436
01:00:29.760 --> 01:00:29.960
Yep.

1437
01:00:30.600 --> 01:00:34.520
Michael wants everyone to go with him, and he starts to pull at Phyllis' chair.

1438
01:00:34.780 --> 01:00:37.240
And you see it from the point of view of Charles, right?

1439
01:00:37.340 --> 01:00:39.600
You see Phyllis kind of like lurching, right?

1440
01:00:39.880 --> 01:00:40.080
Yeah.

1441
01:00:40.080 --> 01:00:44.900
To the side, if you watch the bloopers, you guys, and I remember this happening.

1442
01:00:45.160 --> 01:00:50.120
The first time we did this scene, Steve yanks on Phyllis' chair, and she fell right out of

1443
01:00:50.120 --> 01:00:50.300
it.

1444
01:00:50.380 --> 01:00:51.040
Oh, yeah.

1445
01:00:51.100 --> 01:00:51.700
I remember that.

1446
01:00:51.700 --> 01:00:52.980
And they didn't stop rolling.

1447
01:00:53.460 --> 01:00:55.880
You know, Michael just goes, oh, my God, Phyllis, are you okay?

1448
01:00:55.880 --> 01:00:56.400
Are you okay?

1449
01:00:56.540 --> 01:00:59.100
And Phyllis kind of snorts, laughs, and she says, yes, yes.

1450
01:00:59.520 --> 01:01:01.560
But it's in the bloopers, and it's great.

1451
01:01:02.680 --> 01:01:05.320
Now, Charles is going to find Michael.

1452
01:01:05.560 --> 01:01:05.780
Yeah.

1453
01:01:05.880 --> 01:01:09.540
He comes out of his office, and they have this really awkward exchange.

1454
01:01:10.080 --> 01:01:11.520
Yeah, like, where it's going to get physical.

1455
01:01:12.000 --> 01:01:12.460
All right.

1456
01:01:12.580 --> 01:01:17.540
In the deleted scenes, Jenna, Charles finds Michael stealing office supplies in a box

1457
01:01:17.540 --> 01:01:19.600
and chases him through the kitchen.

1458
01:01:20.160 --> 01:01:23.100
Michael drops the box of supplies to, like, throw them off.

1459
01:01:23.220 --> 01:01:24.680
You know, maybe Charles will trip over it.

1460
01:01:24.780 --> 01:01:30.280
And then he, like, last-ditch effort, just grabs the big container of cheese balls and

1461
01:01:30.280 --> 01:01:31.320
makes a run for it.

1462
01:01:31.660 --> 01:01:32.560
Oh, my gosh.

1463
01:01:32.560 --> 01:01:36.680
That's why we're going to have cheese balls later in Michael's paper company.

1464
01:01:37.020 --> 01:01:40.660
Because in the deleted scenes, that's what he leaves with is the cheese balls.

1465
01:01:40.900 --> 01:01:41.660
I love it.

1466
01:01:41.920 --> 01:01:42.300
I know.

1467
01:01:42.420 --> 01:01:43.380
I wish it had made it in.

1468
01:01:43.520 --> 01:01:46.340
So for me, when Michael's like, who's with me?

1469
01:01:46.440 --> 01:01:47.320
Who's coming with me?

1470
01:01:47.420 --> 01:01:49.060
This is his Jerry Maguire moment.

1471
01:01:49.300 --> 01:01:51.780
Instead of a goldfish, it's a bunch of cheese balls.

1472
01:01:52.120 --> 01:01:53.060
That is perfect.

1473
01:01:53.060 --> 01:01:56.160
I thought we had to hear Jerry's moment and then Michael's moment.

1474
01:01:57.660 --> 01:02:06.560
This moment will be the moment of something real and fun and inspiring in this god-forsaken

1475
01:02:06.560 --> 01:02:09.060
business, and we will do it together.

1476
01:02:12.060 --> 01:02:13.060
Who's coming with me?

1477
01:02:14.120 --> 01:02:15.180
Who's coming with me?

1478
01:02:16.660 --> 01:02:17.940
Who's coming with me?

1479
01:02:22.570 --> 01:02:26.050
Who's coming with me besides Flipper here?

1480
01:02:28.170 --> 01:02:29.670
I will go with you.

1481
01:02:29.670 --> 01:02:33.310
And now, for Michael and Pam's moment.

1482
01:02:59.690 --> 01:03:03.790
All right, everybody who's going to go with me, I want you to stomp your foot.

1483
01:03:06.660 --> 01:03:07.240
Oh, no.

1484
01:03:07.520 --> 01:03:07.700
What?

1485
01:03:09.200 --> 01:03:10.060
I'm going with him.

1486
01:03:11.420 --> 01:03:12.600
I mean, come on.

1487
01:03:12.840 --> 01:03:14.500
Oh, it was so Jerry Maguire.

1488
01:03:14.720 --> 01:03:18.560
By the way, I forgot about the goldfish in Jerry Maguire, and I'll have you know that

1489
01:03:18.560 --> 01:03:22.240
when we get to Michael Scott Paper Company, not only do we have those cheese puffs, but

1490
01:03:22.240 --> 01:03:23.740
Michael has a goldfish on his desk.

1491
01:03:23.840 --> 01:03:24.460
Come on.

1492
01:03:24.620 --> 01:03:24.860
Yep.

1493
01:03:25.480 --> 01:03:28.740
Well, fans were very split on this episode.

1494
01:03:28.980 --> 01:03:33.960
A lot of people loved this turn of events of Michael starting his paper company and

1495
01:03:33.960 --> 01:03:39.800
Pam going with him, but other people really thought that it was selfish of Pam to quit

1496
01:03:39.800 --> 01:03:42.020
without talking to Jim firSt.

1497
01:03:42.660 --> 01:03:45.900
Well, we talked to Aaron Schur about this, and he said two things.

1498
01:03:46.660 --> 01:03:54.580
First of all, he said, in a future episode, spoiler alert, Vikram from the telemarketing

1499
01:03:54.580 --> 01:03:57.280
firm is going to join Michael Scott Paper Company.

1500
01:03:57.500 --> 01:03:57.840
Yes.

1501
01:03:58.040 --> 01:04:04.500
He wrote this talking head for Vikram that got cut, but it explained why Vikram decided to

1502
01:04:04.500 --> 01:04:07.900
join Michael Scott Paper Company, and it went like this.

1503
01:04:07.900 --> 01:04:13.320
When you put your telemarketing career on the line, you haven't put much on the line.

1504
01:04:14.040 --> 01:04:17.900
And Aaron said he felt like that kind of summed up Pam as well.

1505
01:04:18.280 --> 01:04:18.960
Right.

1506
01:04:19.320 --> 01:04:22.680
That Pam wasn't quitting much of a job at all.

1507
01:04:22.960 --> 01:04:27.260
Well, if she could be replaced by some invisible scotch tape.

1508
01:04:27.600 --> 01:04:28.200
Yeah.

1509
01:04:28.460 --> 01:04:28.760
Right?

1510
01:04:28.980 --> 01:04:29.300
Yeah.

1511
01:04:30.500 --> 01:04:37.580
There was also a line that Aaron wrote to explain this business of Pam not talking to

1512
01:04:37.580 --> 01:04:43.360
Jim before making this decision, a little couplet of dialogue that got cut, where Jim said

1513
01:04:43.360 --> 01:04:46.140
to Pam, shouldn't we have talked about this first?

1514
01:04:46.480 --> 01:04:50.000
And Pam said, you blindsided me with a house.

1515
01:04:50.420 --> 01:04:50.840
Ooh.

1516
01:04:51.160 --> 01:04:52.780
And Jim said, you're right.

1517
01:04:52.780 --> 01:04:53.980
I'll bring your stuff home.

1518
01:04:54.460 --> 01:04:57.500
So he did address it, but it ended up getting cut.

1519
01:04:57.700 --> 01:05:02.280
I think it was the right move to cut it, because it seems like, I don't know, a real thing

1520
01:05:02.280 --> 01:05:04.440
Pam is holding onto that I don't think she is.

1521
01:05:04.560 --> 01:05:05.540
No, I don't think so.

1522
01:05:05.540 --> 01:05:08.800
As soon as Jim showed her the house, she loved it.

1523
01:05:09.000 --> 01:05:10.440
She felt cared for and loved.

1524
01:05:10.580 --> 01:05:13.900
She took it on, and I think she's been very happy ever since.

1525
01:05:13.980 --> 01:05:18.100
So I'm glad that they didn't pin that as some sort of lingering resentment for Pam.

1526
01:05:18.320 --> 01:05:18.460
Yeah.

1527
01:05:19.280 --> 01:05:21.440
Pam catches up to Michael in the parking lot.

1528
01:05:21.660 --> 01:05:28.420
She says she's coming along, but she wants to be a salesman, not a receptioniSt.

1529
01:05:28.620 --> 01:05:30.340
And Jim's kind of surprised by that.

1530
01:05:30.440 --> 01:05:31.520
He's like, oh, okay.

1531
01:05:32.200 --> 01:05:32.460
Yeah.

1532
01:05:33.060 --> 01:05:37.780
And everyone is gathered again up in the conference room, and they're looking down as Pam and Michael

1533
01:05:37.780 --> 01:05:38.540
walk away.

1534
01:05:39.100 --> 01:05:43.560
And as they're walking away, you can see the doubt.

1535
01:05:43.780 --> 01:05:47.920
You see this change of them being from triumphant to kind of doubt.

1536
01:05:47.920 --> 01:05:48.400
Right.

1537
01:05:49.060 --> 01:05:52.760
Well, a lot of people liken this ending to the ending of The Graduate.

1538
01:05:53.380 --> 01:05:58.980
And spoiler alert to anyone who's never seen The Graduate, but at the end of the movie, the

1539
01:05:58.980 --> 01:06:04.860
character of Benjamin, who's played by Dustin Hoffman, crashes the wedding of his love Elaine,

1540
01:06:04.860 --> 01:06:07.920
and the two of them are running away from the church.

1541
01:06:07.920 --> 01:06:13.120
They're laughing together, and then they jump onto this city bus, and it's always just so

1542
01:06:13.120 --> 01:06:13.600
exciting.

1543
01:06:13.740 --> 01:06:18.220
And they take their seat, and while they're sitting there, their expressions kind of slowly

1544
01:06:18.220 --> 01:06:18.800
change.

1545
01:06:19.240 --> 01:06:20.740
It's a really famous scene.

1546
01:06:20.840 --> 01:06:21.480
It's so good.

1547
01:06:21.800 --> 01:06:27.060
Well, in the script, our stage direction for this scene was this.

1548
01:06:27.460 --> 01:06:30.460
Jim waves as Michael and Pam walk out together.

1549
01:06:30.560 --> 01:06:35.680
We stay on their faces as they transition from fantasy to reality.

1550
01:06:35.680 --> 01:06:39.160
So I was not thinking of The Graduate when we shot this.

1551
01:06:39.340 --> 01:06:44.900
I was thinking of a different scene from the movie The Heartbreak Kid with Charles Grodin.

1552
01:06:45.300 --> 01:06:46.440
Have you seen it?

1553
01:06:46.760 --> 01:06:48.500
I mean, a long time ago.

1554
01:06:48.780 --> 01:06:54.640
Well, again, I guess, spoiler alert, at the end of this movie, he's finally married the

1555
01:06:54.640 --> 01:06:56.080
woman of his dreams, Sybil Shepard.

1556
01:06:56.200 --> 01:06:57.580
He's been chasing her through the whole movie.

1557
01:06:58.220 --> 01:07:05.560
He sits down at a couch at their reception, and then you just see this sort of like malaise

1558
01:07:05.560 --> 01:07:06.920
wash over his face.

1559
01:07:07.160 --> 01:07:08.660
And he's like, what now?

1560
01:07:09.300 --> 01:07:12.280
Because for him, it's all about the joy of the pursuit.

1561
01:07:12.480 --> 01:07:13.920
But now he did it.

1562
01:07:14.060 --> 01:07:14.400
Right.

1563
01:07:14.620 --> 01:07:16.920
And you can tell he's already restless.

1564
01:07:17.440 --> 01:07:21.040
I thought of that moment because I always think that's such a perfect moment of acting.

1565
01:07:21.300 --> 01:07:22.600
I mean, he's so good in that movie.

1566
01:07:22.920 --> 01:07:23.840
But anyway.

1567
01:07:24.220 --> 01:07:29.220
Well, I will tell you that Tom Cruise and Renee Zellweger in the elevator holding a goldfish

1568
01:07:29.220 --> 01:07:30.540
also have a moment like that.

1569
01:07:30.660 --> 01:07:30.980
Hey!

1570
01:07:30.980 --> 01:07:32.960
Because I re-watched the movie last night.

1571
01:07:34.800 --> 01:07:38.320
Well, this episode ends with something I absolutely love.

1572
01:07:38.460 --> 01:07:39.760
There's a conference room scene.

1573
01:07:40.060 --> 01:07:42.500
Charles is telling everyone we've lost some employees.

1574
01:07:42.500 --> 01:07:44.200
We're going to have to do some shifting around.

1575
01:07:45.060 --> 01:07:46.820
And this is so great.

1576
01:07:46.940 --> 01:07:48.480
Everyone's reactions are so good.

1577
01:07:48.640 --> 01:07:49.620
He's like, you know what?

1578
01:07:49.840 --> 01:07:52.320
Kevin, you're going to be answering phones at reception.

1579
01:07:52.600 --> 01:07:54.720
Everyone in the room is like, what?

1580
01:07:54.960 --> 01:07:55.480
I know.

1581
01:07:55.580 --> 01:07:55.840
Kevin?

1582
01:07:55.840 --> 01:07:59.300
I am very much in the foreground of this shot.

1583
01:07:59.440 --> 01:08:03.120
That was on purpose because they wanted me to react, obviously.

1584
01:08:03.740 --> 01:08:09.180
And then he says he's going to put Stanley, who's doing his crossword, barely awake, in

1585
01:08:09.180 --> 01:08:10.160
charge of productivity.

1586
01:08:10.420 --> 01:08:12.120
Dwight is like, are you kidding me?

1587
01:08:12.540 --> 01:08:17.400
Aaron said he pitched that idea of having Charles put Kevin in charge of the phones,

1588
01:08:17.400 --> 01:08:21.500
which is going to pay off beautifully in the cold open of next week's episode.

1589
01:08:21.500 --> 01:08:27.380
But he said it just makes him giggle to think that, like, Charles's big power move after

1590
01:08:27.380 --> 01:08:30.360
Michael leaves is putting Kevin in charge of the phones.

1591
01:08:30.580 --> 01:08:32.480
Like, he's like, I got this place.

1592
01:08:32.640 --> 01:08:33.060
Yeah, yeah.

1593
01:08:33.120 --> 01:08:34.100
I know what to do.

1594
01:08:34.760 --> 01:08:39.380
Speaking of the next episode, ironically, it did not air for two weeks.

1595
01:08:39.760 --> 01:08:40.700
Oh, no way!

1596
01:08:40.760 --> 01:08:42.020
Yes, there was a break.

1597
01:08:42.200 --> 01:08:43.760
I just thought that was really funny.

1598
01:08:43.880 --> 01:08:44.940
People had to really wait.

1599
01:08:45.340 --> 01:08:45.860
Two weeks.

1600
